 No bits within PDIS records are reserved for custom use.  Any record bits listed as WPRI may be used to hold custom fields, with the understanding that they may be reclaimed for standard fields by a future extension.
 
 A custom PDIS extension that alters standard PDIS behavior must be associated with a non-zero value within the designated custom bits in `mpdisctl`.  When the custom bits hold a non-zero value that enables a custom extension, the extension may alter standard PDIS behavior, which may include redefining standard record fields.
